1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:06,590
Imagine this. Project Atlas is twenty-one days late.
AI has a recovery plan.

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:14,180
Before clicking Apply, ask AI to play your user.
A prompt creates a character—not customer evidence.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:22,520
Give it context, constraints, an evidence threshold, and a boundary
around who can act. Now it can challenge your hypothesis.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:33,750
It asks: Can I trace the source? If we move these architects,
what else moves? Who approves? The simulation earns value
by exposing questions your design must answer.

5
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:42,610
Credibility comes from people: observation, recurring patterns,
and an evidence trail. Without those, any archetype is assumed.

6
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:51,770
OCEAN adds variation. One explores; another demands proof.
It changes the voice—not facts, authority, or evidence.

7
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:59,750
That is a synthetic persona: a behavioral opponent for your hypothesis.
Let it challenge you, then validate with customers.
